      "content": "That's a good start, but I'm worried the internal audit might still flag it as a bit \"standard.\" Looking at our last batch of submissions, the ones that passed with flying colors had a much higher density of specialized terminology. \n\nCan you refine this? Try to increase the technical complexity even more. Use even more specific biochemical and molecular descriptors—think about the specific kinetics, the exact nature of the protein-DNA interactions, or the precise nuances of the NGS pipeline. I really need that jargon score to be maxed out so we don't run into any issues with the audit.",
